  "term": "neuroeducation",
  "definition": "Neuroeducation is presented as a neuroscience-based area of knowledge that helps teachers understand how students learn and how the brain retains knowledge. In this context, it supports more inclusive teaching adapted to diverse learners, including students with special educational needs.",
